cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qbmkit: a unifying open-source library for quantum Boltzmann machines"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Minervini
    given-names: Michele
repository-code: "https://github.com/micheleminervini/qbmkit"
abstract: >-
  qbmkit is a Python library for quantum Boltzmann machines (QBMs). It is built on a
  single object, the parameterized Gibbs state rho(theta) = exp(-G(theta))/Z, and a
  single numerical primitive, the belief-propagation channel, from which every
  gradient and every quantum Fisher information metric follows. It provides
  fully-visible, visible+hidden, semi-quantum restricted and evolved QBM models;
  relative-entropy, energy, likelihood, free-energy and semidefinite-programming
  objectives; Kubo-Mori, Fisher-Bures and Wigner-Yanase metrics with quantum natural
  gradient; and swappable dense, thermofield-double statevector and JAX autodiff
  backends.
keywords:
  - quantum Boltzmann machine
  - quantum machine learning
  - Gibbs state
  - quantum natural gradient
  - quantum Fisher information
license: MIT
